Andesite Alloy has at least 4 production methods, only 1 of which is currently available to you!

&a- 1. (Currently Available)&r Use &eBlock Filling&r to directly obtain Andesite Alloy from Molten Iron or Molten Industrial Iron; for details, see JEI or Ponder of Andesite Alloy!
&eThis method allows you to conveniently obtain large amounts of Andesite Alloy without needing to produce Andesite separately! This route will be further upgraded after building the Alloy Furnace — the Alloy Furnace can produce molten metals faster than the Basin.&r

&c- 2.&r Use the Alloy Furnace to smelt crushed ore, producing Andesite Alloy as a byproduct;
&eSince Andesite Alloy is a byproduct, you will need to void fluids to ensure sufficient Andesite Alloy production!&r

&c- 3.&r Recycle Empty Plastic Cans, producing Andesite Alloy as a byproduct;
&eYou need to reach the Moon to obtain large amounts of useless Plastic Cans from Industrial Scrap on the Moon!&r

&c- 4.&r Use the Satellite Station to mine Brass, producing Andesite Alloy as a byproduct;
&eYou need to reach the Moon and develop Desh material before you can use this method!&r
